labyrinth programs vendored for integration testing
=====================================================

the `.in` files in this directory are labyrinth programs sourced
verbatim from the `examples/` directory of the upstream labyrinth
repository:

  https://github.com/m-ender/labyrinth
  copy is at internal/integrationtest/testdata/gems/labyrinth/

each `.in` is the corresponding `<name>.lab` from `examples/`,
renamed so the goruby esolang test harness (which globs `*.in`)
picks them up. the sibling `.expected` files were generated by
running the multi-file interpreter

  ruby internal/integrationtest/testdata/gems/labyrinth/interpreter.rb \
       <fixture>.in </dev/null > <fixture>.expected

under MRI 2.6.10.

omitted programs and why
------------------------

these examples ship in upstream but aren't vendored as fixtures:

- mod.lab, prime.lab, yes.lab -- never terminate under MRI / no
  clean stdout to anchor against (yes is infinite by design,
  prime loops past any reasonable timeout, mod errors on MRI).
- rng.lab -- by design uses Array#sample (math/rand under goruby,
  not seeded against mri's PRNG). the .expected baseline would
  pin one specific random sequence; skip until we share a seed
  or stub sample deterministically.

